<mei xmlns="http://www.music-encoding.org/ns/mei" meiversion="5.0"><meiHead xml:lang="en"><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Pad 47-174-10</title></titleStmt><pubStmt><identifier>https://corpus-monodicum.de/d/a0d846e7-7196-4b94-9fee-83debd72fbdf</identifier><respStmt><corpName role="publisher">Corpus Monodicum</corpName></respStmt><address><addrLine>Domerschulstraße 13</addrLine><addrLine>97070 Würzburg</addrLine></address><availability><useRestrict auth.uri="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/">CC BY-NC 4.0</useRestrict></availability><date isodate="2026-11-04"/></pubStmt><seriesStmt><title>Corpus Monodicum</title><respStmt><resp>Edition (Tropen)</resp><persName>Michael Klaper</persName></respStmt><respStmt><resp>Edition (Tropen)</resp><persName>Andreas Pfisterer</persName></respStmt><respStmt><resp>Text revision (Tropen)</resp><persName>Gunilla Iversen</persName></respStmt><respStmt><resp>Text revision (Tropen)</resp><persName>Ritva Maria Jacobsson</persName></respStmt><funder>Akademie der Wissenschaften und der Literatur Mainz</funder></seriesStmt><notesStmt><annot startid="#m-2faa2c20-e747-458c-9b60-61cdcde99cc2" endid="#m-2679d28c-d25e-49dc-9f8b-8f27d9539a5a"><table><tr><td><rend>((ei))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>semantisch plausibler: ((eis)) (wie ((CT III))).</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-35fe163c-1d81-4a80-84cd-ff2f26d1e42c" endid="#m-0eed6cf3-f295-4fa4-b075-1c345a602b47"><table><tr><td><rend>((homo))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>formal plausibler wäre ((dominus)) (wie ((CT III))); die Lesart ((homo)) ist aber in italienischen Handschriften weit verbreitet.</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-86cc2845-9b97-4658-8e91-4de826ec95bb" endid="#m-3bc6e474-4018-40fc-8069-b0d5822e309b" corresp="#m-comment-2"><table><tr><td><ptr target="#m-comment-2-notes-0"/></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>korrigiert aus</rend></td><td><ptr target="#m-comment-2-notes-1"/></td><td><rend>(wie ((Mod 7)) und ((Bo 7))).</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-ce9d2533-152f-4461-8ec9-7475d581f374" endid="#m-5ad3f28d-22a1-437b-9bb7-9264b90f25ca"><table><tr><td><rend>((Terrigene summi affatur celitus orbis))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>semantisch plausibler: ((Terrigenis summis affatur celicus ordo)) (wie ((CT III))).</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot type="global-comment"><table><tr><td><rend>((15-17:)) Hexameter (((16)) mit metrischen Fehlern).</rend></td></tr><tr><td><rend>Für die Elemente 15-17 sind im Verhältnis zu anderen Handschriften in ((Pad 47)) die Einschubstellen verschoben. ((Bo 7)) hat die normale Folge 18 15 A 16 B 17 C D; ((Mod 7)) teilt das Segment A vor [[aspicientes]]: 18 A1 15 A2 16 B 17 C D. Das je unterschiedlich gelöste Problem besteht offenbar darin, dass sowohl 18 als 15 Einleitungselemente sind, die mit einer Redeeinleitung schließen.</rend></td></tr></table></annot></notesStmt><sourceDesc><source xml:id="wit-pad-47"><bibl><identifier type="siglum">Pad 47</identifier></bibl></source></sourceDesc></fileDesc><encodingDesc><appInfo><application version="0.9.1"><name>Monodi-Zero</name></application></appInfo></encodingDesc><workList><work><identifier>Pad 47-174-10</identifier><title>Hodie redemptor</title><incip><incipText><p>Hodie redemptor</p></incipText></incip><contents><contentItem><locus from="174">f. 174, l. 10</locus></contentItem></contents><biblList><bibl>Ascens intr 18 A 15 B 16 C 17 D (CT III)</bibl><bibl type="printed-edition">II-4</bibl></biblList><classification><termList><term type="genre">Tropus</term><term type="genre">Introitus-Tropus</term><term type="feast">Ascensio domini</term><term type="feast">Messe</term><term type="Editor">Michael Klaper</term><term type="Bezugsgesang">Viri Galilaei (Intr.)</term><term type="Endseite">174v</term><term type="Endzeile">10</term><term type="FestUndGattung">Ascens intr</term><term type="Band_Genre">Tropus</term></termList></classification></work></workList><manifest